  "description": "QEBNET crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H100 N10 O24 Yb4 2+,C1 H8 N3 O12 Yb1,2(C1 H2 Cl2),2(N1 O3 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb7 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb8 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb9 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.437-3.803 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.78-111.58°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb4(L)4(NO3)2(H2O)2][Yb(NO3)3(H2O)2(CH3OH)](NO3)2·4CH2Cl2·6CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
